✅ Fix (Recommended)

Modify that line to only create the user if it doesn't exist.

Replace the line in your Dockerfile (line ~157) with:

RUN id -u ${USER} >/dev/null 2>&1 || adduser --uid=1000 --shell /bin/bash --disabled-password --gecos "" ${USER}
What this does

id -u ${USER} checks if the user already exists

If it exists → skip creation

If not → create user

This is the safe DevOps pattern used in production Dockerfiles.

🔧 Alternative (Simpler Fix)

If ${USER} is always django, you can just remove the UID constraint:

RUN adduser --shell /bin/bash --disabled-password --gecos "" ${USER}

Docker will automatically assign a free UID.

